  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing The Full-Stack Template**\n\nI\'ve been working with this Express + Vite full-stack template. I\'m taking a moment to review how full-stack applications function, especially regarding the `server.ts` file. I\'m focusing on the necessity of updating the scripts in `package.json` when modifying the server configuration.\n\n\n**Analyzing Package.json Scripts**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the `package.json` scripts, specifically the `dev`, `build`, and `start` commands. I\'m focusing on how Vite integrates with Express to manage the development, bundling, and deployment processes. I understand that the `build` script combines Vite\'s bundling with `esbuild` for the server, and the `start` script is critical. It\'s becoming clearer how these commands orchestrate the full-stack application lifecycle. I understand that external accounts like Fitbit need to avoid mock or simulated infrastructure.\n\n\n**Designing The System APIs**\n\nI\'m now designing the REST APIs for the Express server as specified: signup, login, OTP handling, user data retrieval and currency updates, and transaction functionalities. I\'m considering the shift to Next.js, MongoDB, NextAuth, Nodemailer, and Twilio, and how this will affect the development container. I\'m focusing on creating an Express-based server with Mongoose and an in-memory database to allow for easy sandboxing.\n\n\n**Implementing Database Connectivity**\n\nI\'m now concentrating on database integration, focusing on how to seamlessly connect the application to MongoDB. The strategy is to set up an in-memory database initially for ease of sandboxing, and I\'m adding `mongoose`, `nodemailer`, and `twilio`. I\'m going with `bcryptjs` or standard Node\'s `crypto` to avoid any compile issues. I\'ll configure `MONGODB_URI` in environment secrets.\n\n\n"
