  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Evaluating Database Fallbacks**\n\nI\'m currently focused on database fallbacks. I\'ve realized Mongoose can use `process.env.MONGODB_URI`. If this isn\'t provided, I need a dependable in-memory representation or JSON file writing to guarantee data accessibility even if the connection string is absent. This will ensure users always have some data to work with.\n\n\n**Defining User and Transaction Models**\n\nI\'m now implementing the User and Transaction models, focusing on the structures and constraints the user specified. I\'m prioritizing data integrity, defining all standard types in `src/types.ts`. I am considering how to generate the unique account number, sort codes, and handle hashed values like `password` and `otp`. Then, I\'ll integrate this into a fully functional app, ideally with environment variables to connect to a real database.\n\n\n**Designing Server & Frontend**\n\nI\'m now integrating the frontend with the server. I\'m focusing on crafting a streamlined user experience using a Vite React client and thinking through the navigation flow, including client-side routing with clean view states. The pages will include login, signup, verification, and dashboard functionalities, all implemented as smooth transitions using the `motion` library. I\'m aiming for responsiveness and visual appeal in the frontend.\n\n\n**Refining UI State Management**\n\nI\'m now refining the UI state management. I\'ve decided to build a custom React router and context for active routes and user authentication, which allows for smooth transitions with `motion` and avoids React Router issues. I\'m prioritizing direct view state inside React, which is robust. I\'m also confirming we have all requested packages such as `firebase-integration`, `gemini-api`, `image-generation`, and `shadcn-ui`. Since the user specifically requested no Firebase, I am excluding that option.\n\n\n**Implementing Database Fallback Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the local database fallback, and I\'ll display a clear UI warning. I\'ll ensure the local data storage mirrors the Mongoose models\' behavior precisely, which will be a key task. I\'m prioritizing identical data integrity across both MongoDB and the in-memory/JSON-file alternative. I am checking if `process.env.MONGODB_URI` is provided, and connecting using `mongoose.connect` if present. Otherwise, the local db will be used with corresponding warning messages.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will update the `metadata.json` file with a descriptive name (\"AdrieChartered\") and description, as specified by the first turn checklist."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 427195365
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
