  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Project Components**\n\nI\'ve just been looking over the main project components. I\'ve got `src/types.ts` for shared structures, a unified query/repository layer in `src/db.ts` that supports MongoDB and persistent local file fallback, and then a backend with Express routing in `server.ts` that includes fallback logging and lazy loader clients. Now, I\'m thinking about how these pieces fit together.\n\n\n**Defining Frontend Pages**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the frontend pages needed, specifically the ones at `/login`, `/signup`, `/verify-method`, `/verify`, `/dashboard`, and its nested pages for funding, transferring, history, and profile. I\'ve decided on an SPA approach with Vite React, building views in `src/App.tsx` and components in `/src/components/`, or handle it cleanly. Next, I\'m thinking about how the front-end handles authentication and page states using a state machine.\n\n\n**Implementing UI View States**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `activeView` state mechanism.  Upon logging in, I store the `tempUserId` and redirect to the `verify-method` view.  This `activeView` directs the UI card, from `\"login\"` to `\"profile\"`, including those like `\"fund\"` and `\"transfer\"`, using an SPA approach with direct control and preventing router desyncs, all with the `motion` library for animations.  I\'m also verifying the light blue and white color scheme in Tailwind.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view the current `/src/index.css` file to see how styles are loaded before making modifications."
