  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Define App Views**\n\nI\'ve decided to tackle app views by first designing the React context. This context will be responsible for providing all global hooks, managing loading states, handling auth headers, and providing routing helpers. My initial thought is to place this context within `/src/context/AppContext.tsx`, but I\'m also considering creating it as a shared module instead.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the React context `/src/context/AppContext.tsx` to handle authenticated profiles, mock session states, dynamic toast dispatches, API routing configurations, and local storage state persistence. This encapsulates core operational business logic away from page UI components for perfect separation of concerns."
