  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Summarizing Project Success**\n\nI\'m thrilled! The system boots and executes perfectly. Now, I\'m focusing on crafting a succinct and polished overview of the implemented design and functionality, adhering to the specified summarization guidelines.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the full-stack UK online banking mobile-first web application, **AdrieChartered**, utilizing a robust Express + Vite architecture that seamlessly supports Mongoose/MongoDB connections while maintaining safe local sandbox file persistence.\n\nHere is a functional and visual design overview of the implemented platform:\n\n*   **Visual Direction & Brand Identity**: Styled with a professional light blue tone scheme (`#4A90D9` and `#E8F4FD`) paired with clinical white fields and generous negative space to cultivate trust and clarity. Incorporates standard *Inter* system typography for responsive readability alongside *JetBrains Mono* to emphasize security references and transaction details.\n*   **Dual Database Adapter (MongoDB & Sandbox File Persistence)**: Implemented an adaptive storage layer. If a live connection string is available in environment secrets, the platform uses Mongoose to interact with MongoDB. Otherwise, it falls back to a locally persistent JSON database, ensuring that mock profiles, balances, and ledger logs are fully retained across hot-rebuilds without crashing.\n*   **Two-Step Identity Verification Flow (OTP Method Selection & Verification)**: \n    *   **Sign-Up & Login**: Once credentials are created or validated, users land on a masked destination selector (`/verify-method`) where they pick their delivery option (Email via Nodemailer SMTP, SMS via Twilio, or WhatsApp via Twilio Business API). \n    *   **Verification Grid (`/verify`)**: Dispatches a 6-digit code. In sandbox mode, codes are also printed in the server logs for easy testing. The verification grid supports auto-focusing on typing, automated backspace formatting, immediate submissions on the 6th digit, and a 60-second recovery countdown.\n*   **Account Dashboard & Electronic Inward Deposits**: Offers a premium UK bank card layout featuring masked account numbers (`\342\200\242\342\200\242\342\200\242\342\200\242 \342\200\242\342\200\242\342\200\242\342\200\242 XXXX`), formatting-validated Sort Codes (`XX-XX-XX`), and real-time balances. Users can credit mock accounts instantly using a dynamic deposit overlay supporting any preferred display currency.\n*   **Payee Outward Transfers & Debit Alert Templates**: Provides a domestic outbound transfer utility. Users select payees across registered UK institutions (e.g., Monzo, Revolut, Barclays, HSBC) and execute transactions securely. On completion, it displays a detailed receipt card carrying unique tracking references (`ACB-2026-XXXXX`) alongside rapid share actions to dispatch pre-filled alert texts via SMS or WhatsApp.\n*   **Auditable Ledger Statements**: Includes a searchable and paginated history feed configured with Credit\360\237\237\242 and Debit\360\237\224\264 indicator tags. Users can query transactions by keywords or filter by type.\n*   **Settings & Currency Profiles**: Features an initials avatar block. Users can tap to copy card coordinates instantly to their clipboard, see their registration date, or update their default display currency across 15 international codes. All states are updated dynamically across the local backend profile model."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 548803445
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
