    summary: "The error message \"Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter\" indicates that you are attempting to assign a new value to the `window.fetch` property, but it is a read-only property in the browser\'s `Window` object. This means it has a \"getter\" that allows its value to be retrieved, but no \"setter\" to allow its value to be changed directly[1][2][3][4][5]. This is common for native browser APIs to prevent unintended modification.\n\nThis error typically arises in a few scenarios:\n\n*   **Attempting to Polyfill `fetch` incorrectly:** If you\'re trying to provide `fetch` functionality for older browsers that don\'t natively support it, you might be trying to directly assign a polyfill to `window.fetch` without checking if it already exists or in an environment where it\'s not writable[6][7][8].\n*   **Overriding `fetch` for custom logic:** Developers sometimes try to override `window.fetch` to add custom behaviors, such as logging requests, modifying headers, caching responses, or handling errors globally[9][10][11][12]. Directly reassigning `window.fetch` will trigger this error in modern browsers where it is read-only.\n\nTo work around this limitation and achieve the desired behavior, consider the following approaches:\n\n1.  **Use a `Proxy` Object for Interception:**\n    A `Proxy` object can wrap the native `window.fetch` and intercept its calls, allowing you to execute custom logic before or after the original `fetch` request without directly reassigning `window.fetch`. This method is suitable for adding \"hooks\" to the `fetch` API[9].\n\n    \n\nSources:\n[1] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG9TnJwlgjdp-bXnlFgxq5ERWbKnCcGqc9-H9bxGY0NHEL3PvVmUniwd9PUBO2Mz6IAMRjgv-oChs5cJXBF65zK9Ggn4bBzDzVW_NwHIAoOeqypRbx7SRKE8qpPdUifid6KplI9mw3JR0Rmlei4obACjLG91Kd4H43tuasdQexewUsvmPim-5iFB0Vnr8935s9TXWjhOcVtu5gjw6fWnJGLLKxSmJ7Ae1t9tWL_PRwwxg==)\n[2] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFkurGjKiDgTfTY_JBluCX3huieG55ZafWYvLJ0zNJlzKZzF5rM3D7Gg2wyKiIZ4yt_yT_pu-cmj3ORmCplvgY0AgFZ-WFQOyO_YnzVtO1pjX69NM5zvsab6tB5HoagwhBqzCwR2ZrUR9B9LcMq--ccw5spCjcwGF6RS9RoXKVlDudN7NBckzx-IpkRExrkbaPYWXmiVdGkHXcyWrJlhzJV)\n[3] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFjQHWkTQIzac-k_AM-TM5sokQG-jljTq5UrFQBWYZcgBD-P_g8WXfPO7D3RfzJ41MpnRWqnefMgy2YSFF0dQFYMDOk39HxLCtxBI2pIhRQN0TzdubvJUM6bhjoxDeUiF9eFNAIaq5IReNaJ5g8VhSw0jD1l2B-HGTc6ManeMQChGfYl5x9KgzOz7oIVrz_4hHm8A==)\n[4] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFum6wVefHJtRibAroTyxl41DfKURBoqSH4HtJt9UJpERF7nfZJaFJexp01lyRvlt_E12WlWYosWrH9GuCjfsKxn03YFYQ9fzj0irSr-gqpbC4Gx3UdY2RHySrbJWkIiMoOEuVnY9A=)\n[5] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGRO3dyMCoLQYiHO2MoUhKmqxCWzx374SF4ovK8H-vV7Rl_rvE0xZ94RyX8U4zXsZwA6bwQBcgvmK5lyFHC49v3c1c-Mtp9W4GTjxxTCQuVyg8s6iPLEuqXOY42dwdIAZXKFFB-i3s=)\n[6] [ourcodeworld.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHLt1TW2UKwbsBCSZ_1xT34f_TBPhSIkADGj8AajEEqgOrDuGl896lUmD4QF6XmgCxgCfrPrU9XwkII_oSF8G6GxCo_SrJmKBNo-Bq0jwiW0pKKpJ65CgKLhJcfGsrHzRaUVBo1wQgurz-1abubvevc1GL8l_WMAF6wCC86uiGnpcGcdqv_f-QJHMJa2CzBcFtTzl84cO_h)\n[7] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFZAMZq8GNrin0N0yT7TN1Eep7TuAK1ngzH1sTznrfz5V9wpIWDtbngAv84dQqGn37A-4W7nQ9IN37l3tuHj9wTenRTkB8R3S63kyLg6n2PhEbsODA2l0ky6ZqNcljcHupwurz4443nLBYCycJVJK5FehHwmhCCB-xFs3QXYXS4oTD5LBRgwIHABN3b2gHSUxS6DnZm859yHbdL0Lc3p39dwoMZkw==)\n[8] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF_rXurx0m5tCJCXKYNAgaEcJTEmo0WYEJ9kBXGChlNmJilYdKCz9gj08MTy31uUX3uWbVtp7J344GWk5H0gOEvEXweOGo4KmHtRKXVjuw5nKXsSV1t5ZXm8hiIRBVNavHXIn912Mx1_flGMp_oXA8c)\n[9] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG_s-IngE5MMQJuN2do6f7QnF9QRCDOaiHyJp3a3SscGw34yGGXOn7v-I27_A