    summary: "The error message \"Cannot set property fetch of #<Window>\" or its variations like \"Cannot set property \'fetch\' of\" or \"Cannot set property fetch of object\" typically indicates an attempt to assign a new value to the `fetch` property of the global `Window` object, which is usually a read-only property in modern browser environments[1][2][3][4]. This means the `window.fetch` function, used for making network requests, cannot be directly overwritten or redefined by simple assignment.\n\nThis error is a specific instance of a `TypeError: Cannot set property \'<property>\' of undefined` or `null`[5][6][7]. While the general `TypeError` occurs when trying to set a property on a variable that is `undefined` or `null`, the `fetch` error specifically points to a property that exists but is configured to be non-writable (i.e., it has only a \"getter\" and no \"setter\")[1][2][8].\n\nCommon scenarios where this error might occur include:\n*   **Attempting to override `window.fetch` directly:** This is often done when trying to mock `fetch` for testing purposes or to implement a custom `fetch` behavior[9].\n*   **Third-party libraries or polyfills:** Some libraries or older polyfills might try to redefine `window.fetch` in a way that conflicts with the browser\'s native, non-configurable implementation.\n*   **Incorrect testing environment setup:** In testing frameworks like Jest, if `fetch` is not properly polyfilled or mocked, attempts to interact with it or redefine it can lead to this error[9].\n\nTo resolve this, direct assignment to `window.fetch` should be avoided. Instead, if `fetch` functionality needs to be modified, consider using:\n*   **Mocking libraries:** For testing, use libraries specifically designed to intercept and mock network requests, which typically do not involve directly reassigning `window.fetch`.\n*   **Polyfills for older browsers:** If targeting environments without native `fetch`, ensure the polyfill is compatible and correctly initializes `fetch` without attempting to overwrite an existing, non-writable implementation.\n*   **Checking property descriptors:** Before attempting to modify a global property, developers can use `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor()` to check if a property is writable[2].\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGEF9OEfastd7QjUyWe5fbdRJMVvjpbRKTf5cbFXXY1nS1Xu8Fp-zXvmDlxoWciJ-VAbEQGcIEvyLRyw3k2FGb04we_HqQ_30J2fgcgcKxF7i-cenc7rkmqB4f9NlONcwzYWI80tTC4iEBMXZjMDsHm15DVV3BnOI72psgok-XMv2npafYR-VVVpXRhewGE1ZByVzUjaDu3A3VGdp6iQxypnKHwdexJG3I8Dfr9kZAK)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGv1EXgywObTph2rGAyQwFI6TGgMRegn2-0ZLEOyprPGou9TxvbyEeONCVnkNjtNSk04NIu9vhDPMC_-CKIcryhQ0FfUupuVQIsBy5tz02MdW9YvolM_gS004JR90xQr602lzUJV54OTA==)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH5OqOPQhfEhAn7651OxOcYewOHGniEonPDvJV93SGEiWrrMvE7Oim7CsHirae5XM7nBLWAf67zZyWvOQGxfhX4xEAzQMMKffNVRjvPW1Zud4UidNnVXAjUWy7no4_JOZ5aW5r98dC96kVmNQK8Hg==)\n[4] [whatwg.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFFvSjRneLIeOPeXYQSuq76r8TznzHZC3hrWWt75yPYzWRQLUJtgkQ5IIp1JUPqPWmks_0XEvO-ZH59t2h93UQVddL6MAa8vx7db73deHb_HVSZwGzfcts_)\n[5] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGeimNcBU_ucfYm6xBfqpJj3mC2XH0zofaGjzd10auGfBEyIkVbSP5Ffe1_tEUdpExKlOT4Il7TiRx3yUOXzsDNUfLapQD5dLoJBJ59MPHpY3a9UPDn55caxma7hQydNDwBVhPqoo3TCxr4LUXIYbdCUaYodsZ3ZcgikyJYDS1vqafoFVOLk06y8IfdR1AdfYYUeEg3mewIJhaV1XDipodSCkWUvxXuPUvSEpgotkXy)\n[6] [kinsta.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE9j2dM7msWSh2gtK6VFrHFqGgPpO4zOXlbfEgxQT88CJo-kRknIQxarIhctux9COXYt0o4y9gNNJEkDKJ6nGfUMtVGtb2oviC5ylhGEn7k9ejCCYXwGNS6pqlTMQgyZfV8L56uSXF9ttGgTdbfWn0hBgO5Y89rjBi3)\n[7] [geeksforgeeks.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH4QwGE3fB_PVnDA3Y8EcO3Z4mipkgA0_Iu07vIXdNx