    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGeGDujZaTSfIb6Qa2Dev7Tc2kBDJIAlkgeHOd1JfuRRPX3o--qZaWfk_g2NnhuDX3UvxZBEwpxmNeKB5BxCaZKZBbbybu7GD89dO7m1JBTS68iUHnTlFRy-NDXZ5Kfou09tH_RKRdKuUDoOMc-8FsrHln_dNi4bSPIQlJeQb2iicKdh3LXtQ0DVjlaeMBEegN3qj0xiMUD8GlYpk2GDPFAF9_Lvbg8DKUYPSqN_Pa-FsYlLL0e7LtlDWYksFZepAgWFEhoYcE="
      title: "google.dev"
    }
    summary: "The error message \"Cannot set property fetch\" \"getter\" typically indicates an attempt to assign a value to a property that has only a getter defined, and no corresponding setter. In JavaScript, properties can be configured with getters (to retrieve a value) and setters (to assign a value). If a property is defined with only a getter, it is considered read-only, and any attempt to directly set its value will result in a `TypeError`. This error often occurs in strict mode, where classes are always executed[1][2].\n\nCommon scenarios and contexts where this error appears, particularly concerning \"fetch\" on GitHub, include:\n\n*   **Overriding `window.fetch`**: The `fetch` property on the `Window` object is a native browser API and is often implemented as a getter-only property. Developers or libraries sometimes attempt to directly override `window.fetch` (e.g., `window.fetch = some_function;`) for polyfilling, mocking, or interception purposes[3][4][5][6][7]. Since `window.fetch` is not designed to be directly assignable in this manner, such an attempt throws the \"Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter\" error[3][4][5][6][7]. A GitHub issue for `Tencent/vConsole` explicitly mentions this error when `vConsole` tries to directly execute `window.fetch = ...` during initialization[5].\n*   **Missing Setters in Custom Classes/Objects**: If you define a custom class or object with a getter for a property (e.g., `get myProperty() { ... }`) but omit the `set myProperty(value) { ... }` method, any subsequent assignment to `myObject.myProperty = someValue;` will trigger this error[1][2].\n*   **Constructor Conflicts**: Sometimes, a class\'s constructor might try to set a property that also has a getter defined on the class. This can lead to a conflict or an infinite recursion if not handled by using a different internal property name for storage (e.g., `this._myProperty` instead of `this.myProperty`)[8][2].\n*   **Google AI Studio/Gemini API Usage**: Several users have reported encountering this specific error (\"Uncaught TypeError: Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter\") when working with Google AI Studio and the Gemini API[3][4][9][6]. This suggests potential issues with how these platforms or associated SDKs might be interacting with the browser\'s native `fetch` function.\n\nTo resolve this error for custom properties, you typically need to define a setter for the property you are trying to update or store the actual value in a separate internal variable that does not conflict with the getter[8][2]. When dealing with `window.fetch`, direct assignment is generally not the correct approach; more sophisticated methods like intercepting requests or using specialized libraries for mocking/polyfilling are required[5].\n\nSources:\n[1] [mozilla.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE8vykk3LWNnJ9X6058LSCXKA_XDx--ByMVpsO_VdYolhkyPYPDbq6UmCRGXijZW4Frw1N7cOkhePGuWU9HgAoT460yjtYocGXHUVcU4qgET05qreVvC0egYdH48LnFIR8Wt-psuhQvKIOgVaJRreIUQ-gmCSvsDK9in_4CgQdZFV-SY7Pt1wxFZpcOcClN)\n[2] [bobbyhadz.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHhNiswlLIrvs4qlszQvnJR3I3USOPpQNFPmIThsn5Gm6fcseUDsDf3NMzOroXYsARpP2pgS4hnJ9CF6d0ba-muaNG-x5bgl2yk5r4oIV1iTWr2neVB_0W4w7EdPxzboNEj-fbmOi7F1Ev_nUwpw2utEaGqM6xcN1l6hn79HxLp_My0II7bEOzuLg==)\n[3] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG3gaRdB40p-M2R-k-3CShLAkqh1wYuPUgcJlO6wnuJs95f3nYV0NNQuPq3ba20hyEMzf7PVtU5tB2SRYgK9Kj2Pxbe083zVyJpq2p4Pjs9eJrdjLSrkhFbbLpBfEv8eulQ3xmHuB5r0XFdNZIiFWyg9cNT2KwtXXh61JfdFbHFGdcf)\n[4] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGImQ1sSztjMYH5i7aCX2SJMGqycYbHWvO_xQNIXw-248VaDWTGkYHlbm1narmYu7XXJIjj-VXUpJuh-UjM6gCQKeBG904eGYtoXJguq5CsQbgJsYbf1MkeRDy020C6pnBdCXKnezUKzgPS_HxR57Dr8yVG66oBIDSX_HE5NNog9zRaSNhQAoz3UIDeBbPc4uDRoeNQ1qebmpROyhiswJfyiY1g0v6n2R_0YiX1jfdA)\n[5] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGuNffp6ZE43KLoCtba1wbpSmnTZKNqPjnGOEsA8PwsXUIOMZl8ZCCQC7vYE1n5i5agWisfQnQKizw47OuKPy11LBnr9Acv9l9mwjuCFQmb_XttZtIOkTH25CXoJEa4dpq9ryEc7pdq-A==)\n[6] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE8zugAd6qtwWrv7kWCs2gzKJGcIeqCK0Lsz-wXESFf351A5ovCKbb7o-WJHVkP_n-EY19HDlyuvnvRrtGwIiTvfEcFPLKh-ir7HqVodp3yRoOjoyPEqRKS6WCrxMkaR89bw7KQJOvdqUyHTPg9XMNtDRLvt76Vl8xrodjW9NATqG8Ys66gsoEuNZlzgMWfq4KJiV4B-jUDvSNw2NwwBxVKs1a6wI085Gtmmtls7YHm17exzy68HipXKB5w9Pd_WzRj8w==)\n[7] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH7Cjc8lCupERFZ3jc9nlxnHOSHGlICERENYeBLqIqKmIBzwg092yDGIebTjFzwnZWXytr3GpGSizR9tDEfv6aqR2djSDCorP4OFGy0XeTFsI-O_O-DPU18CsqV-5cJ3GmRXaUXRRtaBg==)\n[8] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH7XPQQe_4Owe5u6kD6BqdeH9wv5HqPZAW4JIwCnNLMEYiIwrsU8BmFm8d3-4OSVr0fOdudJMZLhebq4l1ZNDDanM2MhaMK1bIKFdTpQAjrDUGVhX3Ic88WLh7cNl1HK0DbUp2OBECMVqQBNy2obV6fCuOWYtZnKacDT6dFiC5CUQw797wEzS-i4a4EWYjbiBAnmqLrkR1FNLZNi1pSwWU=)\n[9] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGeGDujZaTSfIb6Qa2Dev7Tc2kBDJIAlkgeHOd1JfuRRPX3o--qZaWfk_g2NnhuDX3UvxZBEwpxmNeKB5BxCaZKZBbbybu7GD89dO7m1JBTS68iUHnTlFRy-NDXZ5Kfou09tH_RKRdKuUDoOMc-8FsrHln_dNi4bSPIQlJeQb2iicKdh3LXtQ0DVjlaeMBEegN3qj0xiMUD8GlYpk2GDPFAF9_Lvbg8DKUYPSqN_Pa-FsYlLL0e7LtlDWYksFZepAgWFEhoYcE=)"
