      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHc_2XKqlbphvyUJGHvO9Fpsw88AgYs65wFymaCaKbUdGj4Vqwv6SVPjgMaKvYcWFNH9pAQQi7Wh1aBej3Hs4UP8Mfy0sdCMA2wH7BBVm5iLBGmM9D6_aKgPxCexVmnJfQ-Q24STr7tgpMkUXMf8Jf2J5DRBxltPNPqT8eq6Vk2ulfNwj7w1eax58c9QUyZj_yBD1EncBedeESCMtPYgoItKYI="
      title: "stackoverflow.com"
    }
    summary: "The error message \"Cannot set property fetch of undefined\" or \"Cannot set property \'fetch\' of null\" (or similar variations like \"Cannot set properties of undefined\" or \"Cannot set properties of null\") is a common `TypeError` in JavaScript. It generally means you are trying to assign a value to a property on something that is `null` or `undefined`, rather than an actual object[1][2][3][4].\n\nHere\'s a breakdown of what this error means and common scenarios where it occurs, along with potential solutions:\n\n**Understanding the Error**\nIn plain English, this error indicates that you\'re attempting to do something like `obj.property = value`, but the `obj` itself doesn\'t exist yet; it\'s either `null` or `undefined`[1][2]. You can\'t set a property on something that isn\'t an object[1].\n\n**Common Causes and Scenarios**\n\n*   **Uninitialized Objects/Variables:** This is one of the most frequent causes. You might declare a variable but not assign it an initial object value, or an object might not be properly initialized before you try to access its properties. For example, `let user; user.name = \"Alice\";` would throw this error because `user` is `undefined`[1][3][4].\n*   **DOM Manipulation Issues:**\n    *   **Script Loading Before DOM:** If your JavaScript code attempts to access or manipulate DOM elements before they have been fully loaded and rendered by the browser, the `document.getElementById()` or similar methods might return `null`. Trying to set a property on this `null` result will cause the error[2][5][6][7]. The solution is often to place your `<script>` tag just before the closing `</body>` tag or use the `defer` attribute[2][5][6][7].\n    *   **Spelling Errors:** Typos in IDs or class names when referencing DOM elements will lead to `document.getElementById()` returning `null`, resulting in the error when you try to set a property[2][8][7].\n    *   **Invalid or Non-existent DOM Elements:** Accessing a DOM element that doesn\'t exist in your HTML will also yield `null`[2].\n*   **Asynchronous Data Fetching (API Calls):** When fetching data from an API, the data might not be available immediately. If your code tries to access properties of the fetched data before it has been successfully loaded and assigned to a variable, the variable might still be `undefined`[1][9][4].\n*   **Nested Object Handling:** If you are working with deeply nested data structures, a property at an intermediate level might be `undefined` or `null`, and trying to access a property further down the chain will trigger this error[1][9][4].\n*   **Specific to `fetch` API:**\n    *   **Incorrect `fetch` Implementation in Node.js:** If you\'re using a `fetch` polyfill or an older `fetch` package in Node.js, it might not return a Promise or might expect a callback instead of `.then()`. This can lead to errors like \"Cannot read property \'then\' of undefined\" when trying to chain a `.then()` call, implying the `fetch` result itself is not what\'s expected[10]. Using modern, promise-based `node-fetch` or similar packages is recommended[10].\n    *   **Trying to re-assign the global `fetch` object:** In some environments (like a browser\'s `Window` object), the `fetch` property might be a getter-only property. Trying to directly assign a new value to `window.fetch` will result in \"Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter\" because you can\'t overwrite it directly[11][12][13]. This might happen when trying to proxy or mock `fetch` without proper handling.\n    *   **`this` context issues:** In class components or specific JavaScript contexts, `this.fetch` might be `undefined` if the `fetch` function isn\'t correctly bound to `this` or isn\'t present in the instance[14].\n\n**Solutions and Best Practices**\n\n1.  **Initialize Objects Properly:** Always ensure that variables or objects are initialized before you try to set properties on them. If it\'s meant to be an object, initialize it as an empty object (`{}`)[3][4].\n    \n\nSources:\n[1] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF_JpPaBggDZjpYW-Crcj2tawO39dbqCbdAfpZAht8ljy-4-IWlkCdtg8s1zRwZ3wRiMW76Ywv5W5N5mvYf8O0mnLcElGT4BpXVrQ073J5l2EF1IHO0xXFiynGT8CCL_XeLJ-8QqMJrfkDkP0S8ivw-a3O3xXT4o87ebncitUIpPtQyT_seYdWM8RtVdydTRDxR7c8CBT3nx9AuXbLY7EOewMIcrDr-Nm2UnY8OZ5wmhg==)\n[2] [kinsta.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHjzeuubYKlf2jB82mZ59_nUQxalct3BBnMvoPsoFvjWKVE93MrhgqKFd61m5kaXx14hAF_g13ILcj-NOv556qLdvuRrOWLObhSIVmN3JqmZMDu7c6TC5_2Px3qENuboFQmbdMR1lgZv4V-dOEeIF-VFHujEekKrehZ7Q==)\n[3] [geeksforgeeks.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEzm8qnaNzPoJH_dp2F6tAsWxEra1E52xeqqdulpEaktyE8yzds6903uwFBs0-lWmkAksFGuNouKOH8QbaTncxCYJZSmGllpSoqfzIHdhARr3MooIJlwpN8Tb9b4EnX9qMPC1ntz58yOjOZr8-iKz6ruQlWIYi2uwhzvYhmPlglm_OTTFPHw9bm9dRZJjLXFFSQN6gpw_GUgrqU38gdRVpIBo1xd0W3AQ==)\n[4] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEklsUV1DQAyDpVb_DVaRv1VlpNE7ICZIatl93wPpaV_EulObcJzZJQRDp9zvLVpvsq__M2sJdRkV7M9Ifeq15-9lsvU1QNQTXGTC1G8FVyZJpFyFLEF0OS7GgowfJvoe4gHkww0mWt-HoSV_vPR4ht1DHhhA54mLOx9o_DcSdDC4m0wpKd8GQW7znYFsdnSgAf6fV2pIfkfngG4X1K)\n[5] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFJScUjpUX-IUH9lN8ESLh7sHe3usr19RNY3YvQhD2Y48XMfn62_KJ1a-32CAOuvm_1nBw1sOtxiDJXO9fCyM8O1hYbhyRNyT0OhiTYfc-RuEi4aEBFFL51duy3_syiahNrong3Vkw=)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFi8k2tR_CUYSTcbHxGupYjjO-Oi6XVAmStgvaqqepqcx-dqrUTweWFah-spkCsQRcn7iAcLpTMF8dZmjOgNgRuR6I8q3WJ-oL9MmVtV5WYgn0lQOvN3r74G7frAGYypBJAcyGrUdqbuIRcdXc4QgUBB7uGM1mRh3BmsXt2KH0fj3yh5kLaFdIfiwGc_YJ2qR3ASQQHVaxIQ3KsPVRsjfGzMcxn0jFtFJo6c0p7mS5eVCQ7frvnoQ==)\n[7] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFi41u5K9ldutuw1LHM9wT4Q8e4hx8j9iiUJmvtLdPSI61HPj96wHn-XeMRTgMRBtdMRH-HPmXiXsPCo8e5xfkWCkKWAsSqr-xdg