    summary: "The error message \"Cannot set property fetch of #<Window>\" or \"Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter\" indicates that your code is attempting to reassign or redefine the `fetch` property on the global `window` object. This operation fails because `window.fetch` is a built-in browser API that is typically implemented as a \"getter-only\" property, meaning its value can be read but not directly overwritten by simple assignment[1][2][3][4].\n\nIn modern web browsers, the `fetch` API is a native feature that provides an interface for fetching resources across the network[5]. It\'s designed to be robust and not easily tampered with, which is why its property on the `window` object is not configurable for reassignment[3][4].\n\nCommon causes for this error include:\n*   **Polyfills or Libraries** Some third-party JavaScript libraries or polyfills might try to provide their own implementation or shim for the `fetch` API. If they attempt to assign to `window.fetch` in an environment where `fetch` is already natively supported and protected as a getter, this error will occur[1][3].\n*   **Browser Extensions** Malicious or poorly developed browser extensions can sometimes interfere with native browser APIs by attempting to modify them, leading to such errors[1].\n*   **Developer Code** Direct, unintentional attempts in your own JavaScript code to assign a new value to `window.fetch` (e.g., `window.fetch = myCustomFetchFunction;`) will trigger this error.\n*   **Bundler or Build Tool Interactions** In complex development setups, especially with frameworks like Next.js and bundlers like esbuild or Webpack, there can be scenarios where third-party libraries are bundled in a way that causes them to try to reassign `window` properties that are getters. This has been observed with various `window` properties, not just `fetch`[6][3][7]. Strict mode in JavaScript can also make these errors more explicit[6].\n\nTo debug and resolve this error:\n1.  **Identify the Source** Use your browser\'s developer console to examine the stack trace associated with the error. This will help you pinpoint the exact line of code or script that is attempting to modify `window.fetch`[1].\n2.  **Check for Conflicting Libraries** If you are using any `fetch` polyfills or network-intercepting libraries, verify their compatibility with modern browsers. Ensure they are either conditionally loaded (only when `fetch` is not native) or configured correctly to avoid overwriting the native API.\n3.  **Disable Browser Extensions** Test your application in an incognito window (which typically runs without extensions) to see if the error persists. If it resolves, a browser extension is likely the cause[1].\n4.  **Review Your Codebase** Search your project for any direct assignments to `window.fetch` and remove or refactor them. If you intend to mock `fetch` for testing, use a testing utility designed for this purpose, as they typically employ more sophisticated methods than direct assignment to safely intercept network requests.\n5.  **Examine Build Configurations** If you\'re using a build system or framework (like Next.js), investigate how it handles third-party module imports and global object modifications. Some workarounds might involve adjusting import statements or specific bundler configurations[6][3][7].\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEdTk5KEXi5NRx5YcC6dE7XuwN_dsGlAUCbaAMJgG9vbW3Fq11MxxfHiZhjYiouPX4AOaEtyvg4GxH8_xfCj8V4Uq_5W0x5nyTDO78us43n-qgbpZjvuI0DqPD5EGx6tINtS3h9b4afLdv2mLDFm8FoPGg3V9BCa54S-CpHErDHBo39SA0pMvpjMiGjD7dE-34pzDL8fSwVt_qxFk-LZglbzhL16-YBxQAvYqnmPJUBCQ==)\n[2] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFcPkh9i-eYm0xkdHzF_wdZjD5UBlKRV17p9dNGFpQlb71K3iNK3aUzb4onoAvYx0Mr4W-LtSE0UajBdW_47C7_ANTSnsiO0mI0cpyOTzO3O7YQgy598kY2MbyjQmvZbsV4zQXDs2rFkcsZg_NlBiVJV_ItgOrTycCYksQZmsGGuzSiAGfDDyQwMAhhfu7bC0KlWxu0AmXGekT-X5rNrMyg)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG8PXIymYJ4I7DOr23V71pPQmlPh08s6L4Os7uWphgmXTDXeRWhY7Qs8AzOsdKbAI1O5Dq09peDoVr6xFsHmDBlgNUoGhW2alobfKs7GTuAkXESoCiMP9myPCtt9HuEJj_93n8fEJE=)\n[4] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEHeBd4k9nQZmjKUfmloEggthV_8IeTJ8dak7ORixPSOwJiL37YDQeEJWZlJdvM2mqxMrmXLATD9_THc_J9OyVWgd1zLJbv05Q_IrO0gz0nV6yqLDpog3AadbxGRvJaqdZ1XoVvfiE62r_zVBHhJPjsos5xoWLtlpt1RlHg9x6O9XQaknqUqNw0Ub5enw==)\n[5] [mozilla.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFd59o-6tQ8zqwNq3ootZJYUPdRAoiufvyJWRngv0XW6UJi0r0ztPT34zY4u-k8WcC6LGOpEGY-U9D1k9hyryPjOeXjZK4Feq9tH8CkhFgSbpnhQrWlor5JiAjOcpwhXOhFEy42cJ8sG5PX9k1auqmTthuWhCOv7NU=)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEM1_ncPYrmwa-PbQE684KvXKpfDq2gKr1JxKx8mMixycxxM-zEolXeMlzkGVkEwVYcxFAzf-to_R3QnLxr1YHvVwPEPu9YacqzbWTvdlTotGrumL_6MdNaVL7ij8zTHynqb15xRpOK8igVQ56ph68LQF9LSxWp-E4B6H6zmADo_d_wZpEv6cx3aZ3M9oU4bi4zbu4NGxJ-aR979lLekOWbhEzjl6xzStpgZXARzL8iuxos)\n[7] [openzeppelin.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGytfPDC6ZS5ugMMLdIt20o2pH_PtnCLDG7ubN5VHcxyGPUEqhqgSwFWl__LQSt_QWf1-XIPfJSO9D_ZYhRaa7_FEInkvTuQH8AQqPRnTcdJzSShHamOueClYobkroakKG5YnGhlMn9LuDv-Q1SiU64tc041ykIUY6lTlrF1XF-mCWfhHfzfSknHpneMt2GXj23iuEQFpuPSl4ihVkWHynEzbz48LOJKCnEh9PwzdgoTtcWUwt--aUBht5L2g==)"
