    summary: "The error message \"Cannot set property fetch\" typically indicates an attempt to assign a value to the `fetch` property of an object, which is either `undefined`, `null`, or a read-only property. This error commonly manifests as \"Uncaught TypeError: Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter\" or \"TypeError: Cannot assign to read only property \'fetch\' of object \'[object global]\'\"[1][2][3][4].\n\nHere\'s how it relates to the keywords provided:\n\n*   **AI Studio:** Users have specifically reported encountering \"Uncaught TypeError: Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter\" when developing applications in Google AI Studio and attempting to utilize its models. This suggests a potential issue within the AI Studio environment itself, possibly related to how it manages or sandboxes the global `Window` object and its native APIs, particularly after migrating to AISTUDIO servers[1][5].\n*   **`iframe` and `sandbox`:** These HTML elements are highly relevant to this error.\n    *   **`iframe`**: When JavaScript attempts to modify properties of an `iframe`\'s `Window` object, or if the `iframe` itself is not fully loaded when the script runs, it can lead to \"Cannot set property\" errors. This is similar to issues where `iframe.src` or `iframe.href` cannot be set if the `iframe` element isn\'t properly defined or loaded[6][7][8].\n    *   **`sandbox`**: The `sandbox` attribute on an `iframe` imposes restrictions on the content within it for security reasons. An `iframe` with an empty `sandbox` attribute will be fully sandboxed, preventing JavaScript execution entirely. More specific `sandbox` flags can allow certain functionalities while restricting others. Attempting to overwrite the native `fetch` API within a heavily sandboxed `iframe` environment is highly likely to trigger this error due to security constraints that make `Window.fetch` a read-only or getter-only property[9][10].\n*   **Vite:** While not directly tied to a \"Cannot set property fetch\" error, Vite, as a modern frontend build tool, can be involved in scenarios that lead to similar property assignment issues.\n    *   Vite uses ECMAScript Modules (ESM), which always operate in strict mode. If code attempts to redefine properties in a way that is incompatible with strict mode or with immutable properties from ES module imports, it can lead to `TypeError`s related to property assignment[11][4].\n    *   Problems with API data fetching in Vite, often due to incorrect proxy configurations or Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) issues, can result in fetch-related errors, though typically not the \"Cannot set property fetch\" specifically unless a custom (and faulty) `fetch` polyfill or override is being attempted[12].\n\n**General Causes and Solutions:**\n\nThe core of \"Cannot set property\" errors in JavaScript, including those related to `fetch`, generally stems from:\n1.  **Attempting to assign to a `null` or `undefined` object:** The target object for the property assignment simply doesn\'t exist or hasn\'t been initialized yet[2][3].\n2.  **Attempting to assign to a read-only or getter-only property:** Native browser APIs like `Window.fetch` are often defined as non-writable properties to prevent malicious or accidental overwriting[1][4][13].\n3.  **Incorrect script loading order:** If a script tries to manipulate DOM elements or global objects before they are fully loaded or available in the execution environment, it can lead to `undefined` references[3].\n\nTo address this error, developers should:\n*   Ensure that any object whose `fetch` property is being set is properly initialized and not `null` or `undefined`.\n*   Avoid directly overwriting native browser properties like `Window.fetch`. If mocking or polyfilling is necessary, use methods that respect property descriptors or operate within a controlled scope.\n*   Verify the execution context, especially within `iframes` or `sandbox` environments, to understand any security restrictions on global object modification.\n*   In the context of AI Studio, if this is a recurring platform issue, consult their documentation or support channels for known workarounds or fixes[1][5].\n\nSources:\n[1] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHaFWUdEmCRajvWwBLh3n7BIbM9r-z56vJj5M4yrecgqtw8qkG_eSEY8B7x38nbEkor0TFgE7SqUd1xcnrWRDRlMVLuN9Q3l8hJPrFYpHisIL0LJNcEu3yTsrXNaM0wOQEEzl3FXdPJ1VQdqet5bdBX1j4E9mpoUBR-6XHseFtxk3CWzfj9fxO56jkalA9OIREjCW38COvq87ltzEdCTYsyoSIoRqU_XtTGZGq0-HIZ)\n[2] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGhG-TQCqUCqu_t9qGXr1WH9huJLljhnblBUGluQ_r54ZdICOFpwExVlVwXLLHNNxwp_CXw0A5Ew19hX7Iw3Vdkm7oZDW06scrJHTa5wC-LPwQqpsRtMTfAutsysTgIo0xdPv9s4Iw7xSBTfFqNy7napTvPc-3E3RJ7JhS4fIYSb9vnidpEj-wXiCINcU4v46on-LqAHTDzeWIZnS9wctyX3tH7YbOX0R72ohZzLcL7)\n[3] [kinsta.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGEWY0rxR7ox5shA4c1OPmhWfe8PrsP_d_OZQx4pP9OgxFwYlpqPEEPfzR1TpNptNO4yWD0PK6JyAZ1sWKMT4Na6BhM70d_IHdV9KKq3TEnTB0F0m1yLenT4tDaYLJ5RmSJKQ2B8A0-GuxEhK-P2_KXk7m1-pFA_wQK)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGc7HAu_NYgZqtXLDll1CZxF7BrU4KxtCtMuFosXXMqlLAwdVkVWfJ7J2MlZUD9idmnp30uUSlxcj9RdXmL6X31z-KAvuHmGv72X2MH3bJ67OtU1Q_U8_eOsrFWt0NTfvbNKePVXg==)\n[5] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGkrt6kuX95Kz5hCmiiZ_hhg1IQ_PaONZ-2_Mlm9mlg41NNdHHKv6Xk0TrSavTcZyDQWJCr78k9ZRFJoAU7X15774qW3eqzTjrCSekPz0mSYl4RBowKwySh1LZoKaCjYZPgRL7JviPWS4NtZ1L971SQz-Lc7FmhwP_QwaabmlIQ3L8J74Gsq9If5_8nZ70l3N0LI5ah6HUq7wTWYPapHptz1h3bNJ6iODSNSnimFNCN-0h45vXGGWhNYnKeG8n1u8Df2g==)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGc0TxnlBikELC6IM_TNIegkt2HbISLITOPlJ5N9tYk1DaDnShLfQNYnKU2zzbGWcGLtGuqKwfdVttTHEOaevEW03C-_RCFEJiXv5AVbk_lLf3XKWNS3Zc20Eyi6LLiXnJUY8p_X0TP00FrVIUKPI4EdFThg7uNUU5ofSSrVj0rg1-9M9R_iISE7vz