  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have successfully resolved the uncaught `TypeError` regarding the read-only `fetch` property on the `Window` object in the sandboxed preview environment.\n\n### What Was Done\n* **Iframe Sandbox Safeguard**: Sandboxed iframe playgounds (like Google AI Studio) wrap native browser APIs like `window.fetch` using read-only property descriptors. When full-stack dependencies attempt to polyfill or monkey-patch the global `fetch` API, they crash under the strict getter-only restriction.\n* **Property Owenership Intervention**: Implemented a defense script injected inline in the `<head>` of the entry document. This script intercepts native `fetch`, redefining `fetch` directly on `window` and `globalThis` as a **writable and configurable own-property**. \n* **Seamless Compatibility**: By shadowing the read-only prototype property with a fully writable own-property, any subsequent library assignment or polyfill modifications succeed without throwing errors, maintaining pristine application load times.\n\nWith the patch successfully implemented, the application compiles smoothly and the development server has been restarted!"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
