    thinking: "**Considering Clickability**\n\nI\'ve realized the profile circle needs to be clickable! I\'m thinking about how to integrate this interaction with `setActiveTab(\"profile\")` to streamline navigation within the UI. I\'ll need to ensure the click functionality is intuitive and seamlessly redirects the user.\n\n\n**Refining Profile Click**\n\nI\'ve got the profile circle\'s clickability nailed down; it looks elegant! Now, I\'m focusing on seamless redirection. I\'ve located the notification bell in `DashboardView.tsx`. Next, I\'m diving into crafting a slick dropdown menu for notifications, including adding a state variable to toggle the notifications panel\'s visibility. I\'ve also found how to get the unread count and I\'m thinking of an absolute overlay drawer or a standard floating dropdown.\n\n\n**Implementing Notification Overlay**\n\nI\'m focused on the notification overlay design now. I\'m aiming for a `w-96` width with a fixed maximum height and internal scrolling. I\'m implementing color-coded indicators for alerts; red for failures, green for successes, and blue for general information. Clicking a notification will toggle its read status via `markNotificationRead(n.id)`. I\'m also adding \"Mark all read\" and \"Clear all\" buttons, calling `clearAllNotifications()`. The notification icon in `DashboardView.tsx` now toggles the visibility of the notifications, with a visual indicator for unread counts! I plan on rendering the overlay container directly in the header.\n\n\n**Designing Notification Display**\n\nI\'m now making the notification display more dynamic, rendering the notification overlay directly in the header. I\'m focusing on responsiveness, implementing a relative positioning container for the dropdown menu, now with a shadow and rounded corners, just like the existing designs. I\'ve updated the button click event to toggle the notification visibility state, which I can render conditionally. I\'m also now styling the display based on unread counts.\n\n\n**Finalizing Notification Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Clear All\" logic, creating a dynamic display that handles the \"No notifications\" case gracefully. I\'m building out the \"Clear All\" button, ensuring it appears only when notifications exist. I am now incorporating the conditional rendering for the \"No alerts or message notifications\" message.\n\n\n**Styling Notification Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on styling the individual notification elements. I\'ve integrated conditional styling for read/unread states, with hover effects. The notification\'s type (failed, success, info) dictates the color of a small indicator. I am now aiming for concise, aesthetically pleasing display of the notifications.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 917077167
    }
