  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Data Persistence**\n\nOkay, I\'m now exploring the implications of storing signup requests. I\'m leaning toward an in-memory array for speed, which feels simpler, but I want to consider a JSON backup (`adrie_db.json`) for persistence too, just in case. Memory\'s appeal lies in its speed, and it may be perfectly adequate!\n\n\n**Refining Registration Workflow**\n\nOkay, the concept of a pending user queue is solidifying. I\'m focusing on the implementation; a server-side array or schema for pending accounts seems optimal. This will let users register and then display a message like, \"Account Pending Approval.\" I\'m looking at adding an admin page to approve or cancel registrations. I will need the core details required to store a pending account.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoint Behavior**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the anticipated behavior for the `/api/auth/signup` endpoint; rather than creating accounts immediately, it will add entries to a pending registry. The response would be informative: `{ status: \"pending\", message: \"Your registration is submitted...\" }`. I\'m starting to consider how the admin interface will function, including approval and rejection mechanisms, and the associated API endpoints that facilitate these actions.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 252838034
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
