  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Admin Endpoints**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the new admin endpoints. I\'ve decided to move signup registrations to a pending list. Now, I\'m brainstorming the admin endpoints needed to manage that pending list. I\'ve identified the first endpoint I need: `GET /api/admin/pending`.\n\n\n**Implementing Pending Signups**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in implementing the pending signup flow. I\'ve mapped out the endpoints I\'ll need: retrieving pending accounts, approving accounts (which creates them and sends an email), and rejecting signup requests. I\'ve begun integrating the pending signup logic into the existing signup endpoint and will be refactoring that code next. I\'m focusing on ensuring a clean and effective implementation, including a \"pending\" status response to users. I plan to put the endpoints in `/server.ts` around lines 210-218.\n\n\n**Validating New Registrations**\n\nI\'m now implementing the validation rules for new registration attempts. I\'m focusing on ensuring required fields are present and that emails aren\'t already in use. I\'m also including checks for existing pending signup requests and validating the preferred account number to ensure correct format and absence from active and pending lists. I\'m paying close attention to edge cases.\n\n\n**Refining Account Number Validation**\n\nI\'m now refining the account number validation logic. I\'ve integrated checks to prevent collisions with existing active accounts and those in the pending signup queue. I\'m focusing on providing clear error messages to the user if an account number is already in use or reserved. This includes implementing `findUserByEmailOrAccountNumber` to check the active database and `getPendingSignups` to check the pending queue. I\'m also ensuring a consistent response with a 400 error status.\n\n\n**Implementing Admin API**\n\nI\'ve just added the `/api/admin/pending` endpoint to retrieve pending applications and am working on `POST /api/admin/approve` to authorize and provision users. I\'m focusing on error handling and data validation within the new admin API. I am aiming to ensure robust and secure admin functionality.\n\n\n**Verifying Pending Approvals**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `POST /api/admin/approve` functionality. I\'m focusing on ensuring the application still exists, and that the email isn\'t already used. I\'ve added a check for this, and will clean up the record if the email is no longer available. I\'ve also added account number resolution. If none is present, I\'ll generate a unique one. If an account number is present, I\'ll check to see if it\'s available.\n\n\n**Finalizing Provisioning Logic**\n\nI\'m now completing the account provisioning within the `/api/admin/approve` endpoint. I\'ve integrated account number validation. If the provided number is unavailable, I\'m returning a 400 error. I\'m generating a sort code, and proceeding to create the active user, then deleting the record from pending signups. Finally, I\'m composing a welcome email to the newly created user, and handling all responses.\n\n\n**Confirming User Notification**\n\nI\'ve just finished implementing the welcome email logic for new users. The email content reflects account details, including the full name, account number, sort code, and the complimentary opening balance. I\'m focusing on ensuring the email delivers the necessary credentials. I\'m also preparing for final testing and deployment, with all systems confirming the process.\n\n\n**Testing Email Delivery**\n\nI\'ve just added extensive logging to confirm successful email dispatch for approved accounts, including status updates and delivery details. I\'m confirming error handling for SMTP failures, with the addition of mocked SMTP behavior for testing. I\'m now verifying the entire approval flow end-to-end to ensure consistent delivery, especially given recent SMTP issues. I\'m aiming to identify and resolve any email delivery issues before complete deployment.\n\n\n**Implementing Rejection Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `POST /api/admin/reject` endpoint. I\'ve focused on validating the request ID and confirming the application\'s existence. I\'ve also implemented the deletion of pending signup data, along with logging for audit trails. Finally, I\'ve confirmed a successful response message.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 23
      nanos: 559731012
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
