    thinking: "**Designing the Login View**\n\nI\'m now diving into the design of the secure admin login view within `AdminView.tsx`. My current focus is crafting a visually appealing and compliant login interface that will be rendered when the user isn\'t authorized. I\'m taking AdrieChartered\'s compliance guidelines into account, and I\'ve already set the credentials to be `akonam` and `ako123` for the user and password, respectively, for this view.\n\n\n**Refining the Login Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the state variables for authorization, admin name, password, and login error within `AdminView.tsx`. I\'ve added a login form, using the new Adrie logo and fields for the credentials. Now I am using the `handleAdminLogin` function to check user credentials against \"akonam\" and \"ako123\" and will display a success toast upon successful login, or otherwise show an error message.\n\n\n**Implementing Admin Credentials**\n\nI\'ve just refined the admin credentials and implemented them directly in the `handleAdminLogin` function. Now, if the entered name is \"akonam\" and the password is \"ako123\", it\'ll confirm successful admin login. Otherwise, it will provide a clear, concise error message. I\'ve also wrapped the return statement in a check for the `authorized` state.\n\n\n**Visualizing the UI Layout**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual layout. I\'ve integrated the AdrieChartered logo, designed a clear title, and implemented the error display, all wrapped in a pleasant background, making sure to hit the AdrieChartered design guidelines. I\'m aiming for a clean, professional look with the appropriate branding. The login form is now positioned inside the main container.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Login Form**\n\n\\n\\nI\'m putting the finishing touches on the login form now. I\'ve integrated the form elements: the clearance name and key input fields, designed in line with AdrieChartered\'s visual identity. I\'ve also incorporated the error message display, styled with the `bg-rose-50` and `border-rose-150` classes, for a clear and immediate feedback loop. I\'m focusing on ensuring its responsiveness across different screen sizes. I\'ve also added a placeholder text that provides clear instructions.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 207470401
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
