  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Backend Integration**\n\nI\'m now exploring the implications of integrating this change within the backend endpoints, as I did the frontend in `AdminView.tsx` during the last round of thought processing. The prompt\'s emphasis on admin credentials necessitates a more thorough examination of security considerations, so I\'m investigating how to securely handle this.\n\n\n**Analyzing Onboarding Design**\n\nI\'m now diving into the onboarding design. My goal is to craft an interactive, multi-step flow within `OnboardingView.tsx`, mirroring the design assets precisely. I\'m focusing on elegant styling, smooth motion, progress indicators, responsive layouts, connected forms, and the backend integration. I\'ve begun to analyze each step in the second image to create a solid design.\n\n\n**Evaluating UI Consistency**\n\nI\'m now assessing the UI consistency across devices. I\'ve realized the left panel\'s visibility adapts between desktop and mobile; it\'s a permanent sidebar on desktop but hidden or simplified on mobile. This mobile-first design is robust, focusing resources on the active form within the wizard. I\'m taking notes on the Stepper Progress Indicator inside the card container, as well as considering the structure of the registration steps.\n\n\n**Designing Landing Page Elements**\n\nI\'m now focused on the landing page\'s design elements. I\'m prioritizing the main header with bold text and tracking, alongside the subheader in text-slate-500. A central interactive illustration, whether a neoclassical bank or a modern SVG, is next. Finally, I\'m working on the \"Get Started\" button and the \"Log in\" link.\n\n\n**Defining Security Credentials**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining user security credentials for Step 3, which is `Set up security credentials`, or `Verify Identity` with OTP is used. We need to focus on providing password and currency preferences. I\'m designing inputs for `Password`, `Confirm Password`, and preferred display currency (GBP, USD, EUR dropdown). I\'m also considering an optional 10-digit account number field.\n\n\n**Implementing Verification Steps**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in implementing the verification steps within `OnboardingView.tsx`. The design includes two potential flows. One features an OTP verification gate after Step 3. The other shows an onboarding confirmation. I\'m building out the interactive OTP input, complete with countdown timers, resend functionality, and API calls to `verifyOtp`. The visual design is on track with the mockups.\n\n\n**Crafting Account Confirmation**\n\nI\'m now designing the confirmation screen users see after signup. I\'m building out both \"pending review\" and \"verified\" states. For pending reviews, I\'m using a title and subtext, and a checklist, plus an alert box with a button for the login portal. For successful verifications, I\'m including a green check badge with a ripple animation, a celebratory title, the same checklist, and a button to go to the dashboard.\n\n\n**Reviewing Implementation Details**\n\nI\'m now ensuring the integrity of custom compliance features like admin credentials and pending approvals. Sky Blue (`#4A90D9`) is our main brand color. I\'m focusing on \"Inter\" sans-serif fonts, and \"Playfair Display\" for headlines to implement with custom classes. I also discovered that `App.tsx` routes `\"onboarding\"` and `\"signup\"`, and the user goes to `signup`, they can directly start at Step 2 of `OnboardingView`. I\'m going to pay extreme attention to detail, spacing, padding, hover states, mobile layout, and animations in the `OnboardingView.tsx` file.\n\n\n**Incorporating New Assets**\n\nI\'m now integrating new assets into `OnboardingView.tsx`. I\'ve verified that we can reuse the `COUNTRY_CODES` and `CURRENCIES` lists from `SignupView.tsx`, and I\'m ensuring all necessary icons from `lucide-react` are included. I\'m focusing on creating authentic SVG illustrations in-code, including the floating temple graphic, neoclassical temple artwork, and skyline watermark to enhance the user experience. I\'m moving toward writing the file edit to overwrite `OnboardingView.tsx` with this master design, after a thorough review.\n\n\n"
