  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Pending Signups**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got it. I\'m focusing on the signup approval flow. It seems users are initially stored as `MongoosePendingSignupModel` or in `LocalDbSchema.pendingSignups` within a JSON fallback database. These pending signups await administrative approval. The next step is figuring out what happens after that.\n\n\n**Investigating Verification Failure**\n\nI\'m now investigating a user\'s report about a missing verification code during signup. Specifically, the concern is the absence of an OTP code on the \"Verify your number\" step. I\'m focusing on the `OnboardingView.tsx` file, examining lines 158-175 for potential issues within that step. The user also mentions an incorrect superintendent name, so I\'ll also be tracking that down.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Method Discrepancy**\n\nI\'ve discovered the root cause. My previous analysis was correct. The frontend is requesting an OTP via the `\"mobile\"` method, however the `/api/auth/send-otp` route only accepts `\"sms\"` or `\"whatsapp\"`. The code appears to be skipping that request. This is because `\"mobile\"` is not within `OtpMethod`\'s supported methods, which are `\"email\" | \"sms\" | \"whatsapp\"`. This clearly isn\'t handled.\n\n\n**Tracing Pending Approval Logic**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down on the \"pending\" status after signup, and found a critical path. It looks like a \"pending\" status skips the OTP verification stage. When the signup data shows `status: \"pending\"`, the system directs the user directly to the \"Pending Approval\" screen. Consequently, the user bypasses the \"Verify your number\" step and never gets a chance to enter the OTP code. This is definitely a mis-match of the intended design flow.\n\n\n**Clarifying Signup Flow**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the fundamental issue: every signup is being automatically marked as \"pending\". This prevents any user from progressing to the OTP verification step, as they are immediately directed to the \"Pending Approval\" screen. The `/server.ts` file automatically adds all signups to the `pendingSignups` collection. This breaks the intended flow, as there are no active users created. The user is asking \"why is the code not being sent to approve when trying to sign up?\". It appears the signup process is *meant* to trigger a code for verification, but that is not occurring, and this is happening before the \"approve\" step.\n\n\n**Revisiting Approval Process**\n\nI\'m now revisiting the user\'s intended signup flow, comparing it against the \"Pending Approval\" state. The user expects an OTP code for verification during signup, as shown in the Step 3 mockup. However, the existing logic bypasses this step when a user is in a \"pending\" state. This means the code sends a \'pending\' state to the user without sending any kind of verification code. This doesn\'t match the design. I\'m considering whether we should allow OTP verification *before* administrative approval. I am investigating a way to add in Step 4 verification.\n\n\n**Reconciling Verification Steps**\n\nI\'m now integrating the mockup\'s intended flow with the existing \"pending\" logic. The mockups clearly show immediate OTP verification (Step 3). Current logic bypasses this verification, making the signup flow deviate from the design. It seems the code is missing a check to trigger OTP verification if the `status` is not `\"pending\"`. The mockup has no \"Pending Approval\" state *before* verification.\n\n\n**Implementing Verification Before Approval**\n\nI\'m now integrating OTP verification prior to administrative approval. The user\'s query about the missing code is my primary focus. My new plan is to send the OTP immediately after Step 2, \"Continue\". This triggers Step 3 phone verification *before* any \"pending\" status, so the user receives a code, as shown in the mockup. I\'m trying to decide if we verify immediately or we allow them to go to \"Welcome\". The superintendent also requires a name change.\n\n\n**Generating OTP on Signup**\n\nOkay, I\'m trying to figure out how to send an OTP during the signup process, even though it currently puts users in a pending queue. Right now, when a new user POSTs to `/api/auth/signup`, they\'re immediately marked as pending. I need to make a change that sends an OTP *before* this pending status, using `/api/auth/send-otp`. I need to figure out how to do this. I\'m focusing on `/api/auth/signup` in `server.ts`. I want to allow OTP after signup, but before administrative approval.\n\n\n**Prioritizing OTP Sequence**\n\nOkay, I\'m now structuring the signup flow. My plan involves sending the OTP code *before* a \"pending\" state is assigned. I\'m focusing on the POST request, handling the \"Continue / Create Wallet\" step, followed by OTP verification, then *conditional* application of a \"pending\" status. I am working on the \"pending\" and \"approve\" process, but the main issue is, why aren\'t they getting the code when they sign up?\n\n\n**Confirming Step Bypass**\n\nI\'ve confirmed a critical oversight in `OnboardingView.tsx`. When `data.isPendingApproval` is true during signup, the code *skips* Step 4 (OTP verification) and proceeds directly to Step 5 (pending approval). This definitively answers the user\'s question, as the OTP is never sent during signup. I\'m focusing on why we\'re skipping the verification step, while the mockup shows an OTP code verification for every user at this stage.\n\n\n**Integrating OTP Delivery**\n\nI\'m now investigating OTP delivery to pending signups. The challenge is ensuring OTP verification *before* a \"pending\" status. I\'m considering sending the OTP immediately after signup. I am looking at the `pendingSignupSchema` to see where the OTP will go. I\'m checking `server.ts` to see where `pendingSignup` is being stored. I need to make the OTP happen, before they go to Pending Approval.\n\n\n**Refactoring Signup Process**\n\nI\'m now completely restructuring the signup process, as a new database schema is required to implement the OTP sequence. I\'m pivoting. I need to figure out where OTPs should be stored. Right now, there\'s no OTP field on `pendingSignupSchema`. I\'m exploring an alternate approach that avoids the `pendingSignups` list entirely. My new plan is to immediately create all signups as standard users, but with `isVerified = false` and `isApproved = false`. This will enable immediate OTP verification.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 19
      nanos: 22233550
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
