  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Authentication Endpoint**\n\nI\'m currently focused on modifying the `/api/auth/verify-otp` endpoint within `server.ts`. The goal is to make it handle both active users and those with pending signups seamlessly. I\'m exploring the logic flow if a `userId` input is a `pendingId`. I\'m going to determine how the system will look up the `user`.\n\n\n**Refining Signup Verification**\n\nI\'ve refined the verification process for pending signups, focusing on the `/api/auth/verify-otp` endpoint. I\'ve integrated checks for `pendingUser` using `findPendingSignupById(userId)`, and logic to update the signup status upon successful OTP verification, marking it as `isVerified`. The response includes an `isPending: true` flag, seamlessly connecting with the frontend\'s OnboardingView. I have also started reviewing the changes needed to modify `/api/auth/resend-otp` to support these updates.\n\n\n**Revising Onboarding Flow**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the OnboardingView\'s logic. Specifically, I\'m reviewing how the view handles pending user registrations within `handleSecuritySignup`. I need to ensure the correct step flow is triggered when `isPendingApproval` is true. The current implementation skips OTP verification (Step 4) and jumps directly to Step 5, which is not desired! This needs immediate correction to match the expected user flow!\n\n\n**Adjusting OnboardingView Flow**\n\nI\'m making a key adjustment to `OnboardingView.tsx`. When `isPendingApproval` is true, I\'ll update `handleSecuritySignup` to store `data.pendingId` in `tempUserIdState`, and set `isPendingStaging` to `true`. I\'ll call `/api/auth/send-otp` with `userId: data.pendingId` and `\"sms\"` as the method. Based on the mockup (Step 3), the view should prompt OTP verification via SMS. I am leveraging existing `send-otp` logic (lines 161-171), to call `/api/auth/send-otp` with the needed arguments.\n\n\n**Implementing OTP via SMS**\n\nOkay, I\'ve confirmed that using `\"sms\"` for OTP delivery is ideal since the `OnboardingView` has the phone details. I\'m now writing the logic for `handleSecuritySignup` in `OnboardingView.tsx` so that it calls `/api/auth/send-otp` with the pending user ID when `isPendingApproval` is true. My goal is to trigger SMS verification after signup, using the existing `/api/auth/send-otp` logic.\n\n\n**Finalizing Onboarding Verification**\n\nI\'ve just added error handling within the `OnboardingView` to address OTP sending failures. If there\'s an error when sending the OTP after signup, I\'m logging it to the console, and adjusting the flow to handle such cases. Additionally, the signup is now correctly advancing to OTP verification (Step 4) instead of bypassing it when `isPendingApproval` is false, ensuring consistent user onboarding.\n\n\n**Handling OTP Verification**\n\nI\'m now integrating the OTP verification step within `OnboardingView.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the `handleVerifyOtpSubmit` function. This function handles the logic when a user clicks \"Verify & Continue\" on Step 4. I\'ve added error handling for incomplete OTP codes and missing user context. I am ready to fetch `/api/auth/verify-otp` with the provided `userId` and `code`. My next step is to make sure I handle the response correctly, updating the UI based on whether verification succeeds or fails.\n\n\n\n**Refining Verification Process**\n\nI\'m now integrating the `verifyOtp` context function within the `handleVerifyOtpSubmit` in `OnboardingView.tsx`. Previously, I had the wrong approach. I will call `verifyOtp` with the current `tempUserIdState` and the entered OTP code. The UI will then update based on the result. If successful, I\'ll go to step 5 (Dashboard). If not, an error message will be shown.\n\n\n**Clarifying Pending Approval Logic**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the authentication flow for pending users within `OnboardingView.tsx`. I realize directly calling the fetch for `/api/auth/verify-otp` in `handleVerifyOtpSubmit`, bypassing `verifyOtp` is the correct approach. After OTP verification, instead of logging in, I need to direct pending users to Step 5 (\"Pending Charles\'s Approval\") using `isPendingStaging`. This is crucial for pending signup users.\n\n\n**Confirming OTP Verification Process**\n\nI\'m now confirming the logic flow in `OnboardingView.tsx` regarding OTP verification, specifically within the `handleVerifyOtpSubmit` function. I\'m focusing on lines 210-235. My primary focus is to ensure the correct handling of the `/api/auth/verify-otp` response and its interaction with state updates for success or failure, to ensure the next step is 5 in the event of success. I am ready to move forward.\n\n\n**Verifying User OTP**\n\nI\'ve just refined the OTP verification within `OnboardingView.tsx`. Specifically, in `handleVerifyOtpSubmit`, I now directly call `/api/auth/verify-otp` when `isPendingStaging` is true. I handle potential errors (incorrect code, expired) and ensure a toast message appears on success. Upon successful verification, I proceed with the flow and set the correct next step.\n\n\n**Reviewing Resend Code Function**\n\nI\'m now carefully reviewing `handleResendCode` within `OnboardingView.tsx`. My current focus is how this function resends the OTP and how it handles potential errors. I\'m making sure it uses the correct `tempUserIdState` for the resend request, and that error messages are informative. I\'m paying close attention to the existing toast messages for clarity and accuracy.\n\n\n**Examining Resend OTP Logic**\n\nI\'m now deeply focused on the `handleResendCode` function, and how it\'s implemented. I will verify how it interacts with the `/api/auth/resend-otp` endpoint, and whether it correctly manages sending the OTP to pending users. I\'m checking the flow within `AppContext.tsx`, specifically the `resendOtp` context, to ensure the correct `userId` is used. I am also planning on modifying the server-side logic of `/api/auth/resend-otp` to support pending users.\n\n\n"
